 ## Overview
-Convex Object Optimization accelerates sphere tracing through convex objects represented by a signed distance field (SDF) enclosed by a convex bounding volume [S3, unofficial]. It solves the problem of inefficient ray marching when the ray origin lies inside the object, where standard sphere tracing requires many small steps to traverse the interior [S3, unofficial]. It sets itself apart from standard sphere tracing by avoiding internal steps entirely for internal origins, and from gradient-based optimizations by relying only on the bounding volume geometry rather than per-step gradient computations [S1][S3, unofficial].
